  "id": "COMPOUND:4152 - PROTEIN:6293",
  "verbalization": "P-Nitrophenol appears to interact with Dipeptidyl peptidase IX through a series of intermediate targets, including Ribosomal protein S6 kinase 2, Rupicolin B, and Hydroxysaikosaponin c. These intermediates are all known to be targets of P-Nitrophenol, suggesting a potential pathway where the compound modulates the activity of these proteins, which in turn influence Dipeptidyl peptidase IX. The shared interaction with multiple targets indicates a possible mechanism involving the activation or inhibition of downstream enzymes, possibly through a common signaling pathway or by altering the cellular environment. The evidence suggests that P-Nitrophenol may exert its effects by targeting a conserved set of proteins that ultimately lead to the regulation of Dipeptidyl peptidase IX. While the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated, the integrated evidence supports a role for P-Nitrophenol in modulating the activity of these downstream targets, which may be relevant in the context of drug development or therapeutic applications.",
